    <Program class="ca.nrcan.gc.OEE.ERS.ErsProgram">
        <Labels>
            <English>EnerGuide Rating System</English>
            <French>Syst??????me de cote ??????nerGuide</French>
        </Labels>
        <Version major="15" minor="10" build="20288">
            <Labels>
                <English>v15.10b20288</English>
                <French>v15.10b20288</French>
            </Labels>
        </Version>
        <SdkVersion major="1" minor="16" build="20288">
            <Labels>
                <English>v1.16b20288</English>
                <French>v1.16b20288</French>
            </Labels>
        </SdkVersion>
        <Options>
            <Main applyHouseholdOperatingConditions="false" applyReducedOperatingConditions="false" atypicalElectricalLoads="false" waterConservation="false" referenceHouse="false">
                <Vermiculite code="1">
                    <English>Unknown</English>
                    <French>Inconnu</French>
                </Vermiculite>
            </Main>
            <RURComments xml:space="preserve">
                <airSeal>The result of the infiltration test, shows a very hight level of air changing per hour and therefore shows a very poor air sealing of the house. Make your house more air tight, will help to reduce your energy consumption bill and also reduce the feeling of cold that occurs with the infiltration of the outdoor air inside the living space. 



</airSeal>
                <mainWalls>Walls are made by 2x3 R-8, to small, not efficient and cold. An upgrade to R-30 is recommended. The insulation by outside is recommended, it will avoid the  reduction of the interior  space, and will help to seal the exterior walls properly.



We recommend the addition of R-30. Take a special look on the joints and make sure that your air barrier is continous. The more careful you are on the details, the more efficient your new envelope will be.</mainWalls>
                <ceilings />
                <ceilingsCathedral>The actual ceiling is in a bad shape and therefore makes it quite leaky. The ceiling must be repaired.

We recommend the removal of the existing drywall and install a vapour barrier to seal completly the ceiling from the living space. The usage of cawlking for the joints is recommended.



The existing flat roof does not let the addition of more insulation. During our visit the owner mention the idea of installing new trusses over the existing roof. If you do so, you will be able to add more insulation. 



We recommed to reach a level of insulation of R-70, which result in an addition of approximately 14'' (R-42) of insulation on top of the existing 8'' (R-28) alrady in place.</ceilingsCathedral>
                <exposedFloors>No exposed floor, but floor over crawl space need to be repaired. The floor above the crawl space need to be repaired. Sogn of mould and deformation are visible, specially in the bathroom. We recommend the installation of a non permeable insulation materiel and a level of insulation of R-30.</exposedFloors>
                <foundation>No foundation, crawl space. The walls need more insulation and ventilation as well as the floor. We recommend to reach  a level of insulation of R-30 to insulate the main floor area over the crawl space.</foundation>
                <windows>Old single window. Presence of condensation and are very leacky.

The windows are probably the original, the units are very leaky and condensation appear on the glass when is cold outside. This problem lead to mould creation around the frame and air leakage trough the windows.



The air leakage represent one f the main source of heat loss and result in an incresing of energy to heat the interior space. 



We recommend the installation of windows certified Energy Star, Triple glass, with Argon and Low-e. The interior frame must be insulated. This type of window are adapted and better builted to face the northern weather and climate.</windows>
                <doors>Front door should be replaced, very leaky



We recommend the replacement of the main door, by an Energy Star door with window or not. If with window it must be an Energy Star, Triple glass, Argon and the space between the glasses insulated,

 </doors>
                <VentilationSystem>In this moment there is no ventilation unit. Therfore if replacement of all windows and doors, plus the increase of insulation of the exterior walls and floor, will make the house more air tight and can result in an increase of the humidity in the house.



An HRV (Heat Recovery Ventilator) will be probably needed to reduce the humidity inside the house and insure a proper ventilation inside the house.</VentilationSystem>
                <HeatingSystem>The owner mention the idea in replacing the heating system. In this moment the house is heated by an oil furnace.



We recommend the replacement by an electric furnace. This type of unit is 100% efficient compared to natural gas or oil furnace. The units working with fossils fuels can't be 100% efficien due to the combustion and required combution diluation air coming trough the envelope.</HeatingSystem>
                <CoolingSystem />
                <Renewables />
                <WaterConservation>Replacing the existing toilet for a low flow toilet can contribute to reduce your water consumption.</WaterConservation>
                <AdditionalComments>This house was not veryn well maintained by the previous owners. Perhaps some works are required to make the house safe to use, confortable for the owners and up to code.



</AdditionalComments>
            </RURComments>
